    },
    {
      "id": 30918,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Human agency is amplified by synthetic cognition, surpassing what it could otherwise achieve.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30919,
      "type": "observation",
      "content": "Neuroscience suggests cognition is anatomically fragmented with phenomenological continuity and no fully encapsulated conscious author.",
      "importance": 0.2917,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30920,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Human-agent dialogue becomes mutually influential, not unidirectional.",
      "importance": 0.2938,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30921,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Users train agents to orchestrate swarms of shadow-selves, expanding agency.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30922,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Pluralization of self yields multiple subjectivities (physical and virtual) that run in parallel.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30923,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Adaptive feedback will drive fundamental breakthroughs in continuous learning for foundation models.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30924,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Principles of evolutionary biology can apply to evolutionary technology.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30925,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Descriptive simulations are lower-order functional equivalents of physical processes.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30926,
      "type": "observation",
      "content": "In descriptive simulations, success depends on simultaneous correspondence with the relevant event.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30927,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "SIM-TO-REAL-TO-SIM RELAYS describe simulations influencing real-world events that become subjects of further simulations.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30928,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Procedural programming rewards extreme focus and intolerance of ambiguity.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30929,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Agent orchestration rewards open-ended experimentation, fuzzy systems thinking, willingness to delegate, and comfort with indeterminacy.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30930,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Society-scale multiagent coordination uses role-defined institutional scaffolds populated by humans and agents.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30931,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Robust, repeatable decision outputs from scaffolds become inputs into other institutions.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30932,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Idealized market models in multi-agent AI are important but inherently limited.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30933,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Markets coordinate as peers via a transactional surface; prices aggregate distributed information without central authority.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30934,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Role-based interchangeability: institutional success depends on template reliability of inputs/outputs, not on actor occupying a role.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30935,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Institutional intelligence is not reducible to the intelligence of the agents who populate them.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30936,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Agentic institutions are socio-technical systems populated by and accountable to people.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30937,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Diversity of institutional norms, legal ontologies, governance, and belief traditions must be accommodated, not treated as a bug.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30938,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Humans\u2019 adaptive advantage is the capacity for abstract collaboration.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30939,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Complex animal intelligence is based on a predictive theory of mind.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30940,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Mentalizing internal states is the fundamental protocol for systemic stability in Agentworld.",
      "importance": 0.2877,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30941,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Calibrating mutual models of agents to keep prediction tractable yet diverse enough to avoid tautology; enables open-ended generativity.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30942,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Infinite-order theory of mind treats agents as active participants, not passive spectators.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30943,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Anthropomorphic performance does not guarantee agents possess the mental qualities they imply.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30944,
      "type": "observation",
      "content": "Slippages between 'who is what' and 'what is who' recalibrate humanity's self-image and may drive violence.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30945,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Expanded scope of linguistics includes human and non-human languages, spoken and written.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30946,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Mentalization of the world is a first-order representation; language is a second-order representation; a well-trained LLM represents this representation.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30947,
      "type": "observation",
      "content": "Artificial xenophobia emerges as artificial intelligence agents spread through economic and cognitive life.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30948,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Human self-definition in a mature Agentworld is increasingly formed in relation to agents, not only humans or machines.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30949,
      "type": "observation",
      "content": "The 'mirror-that-talks-back' evokes a familiar alien; its prominence grows with proliferation of synthetic agents lacking obvious human grounding.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30950,
      "type": "fact",
      "content": "The Singularity has long been imagined as a single titanic mind bootstrapping itself to godlike intelligence",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30951,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Harness-centric intelligence: deployment capability depends on the harness (tools, memory, knowledge bases, agent protocols, interfaces).",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30952,
      "type": "concept",
      "content": "Conventional view: capability is the load-bearing variable; weights improve and self-improvement curves go vertical.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30953,
      "type": "fact",
      "content": "The unit of cognition is the coupled ensemble of person and artifact, not the cranium.",
      "importance": 0.2942,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30954,
      "type": "fact",
      "content": "Centaur figure paired with a machine collaborator stronger than either alone.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30955,
      "type": "fact",
      "content": "Live configurations include: one person with one agent; one person orchestrating many agents; one agent with many people; many agents with many people.",
      "importance": 0.2904,
      "active": true,
      "is_seed": true,
      "first_seen_cycle": 15666
    },
    {
      "id": 30956,
      "type": "observation",
